==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|zwō}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} *''tw(a)ōz'' (see {{m|gem-pro|*twai}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}}. ''Zwo'' is originally the feminine form, but is now used as a variant of {{m|de|zwei}} without gender distinction. Compare, however, {{cog|lb|zwou}}, which is still a feminine form of {{m|lb|zwéin}}. The same is true of some German dialects, e.g. in Switzerland. More at ''[[two]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/tsvoː/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-zwo.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Numeral===
{{head|de|numeral}}

# [[two]]

====Usage notes====
* {{m|de|zwei|Zwei}} is the usual German word for "two", but {{m|de||zwo}} is sometimes used as more clearly distinguishable from {{m|de|drei||three}}, especially over the telephone and in military parlance. Outside of these contexts, it is used chiefly in southern Germany and Austria.

